{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y4TPT4uDwWs3CtfLArz2ia","type":"tool_result","content":"The error stays hidden until the field is blurred once, then updates live,\nand the submit button is disabled until valid. See `example/subscribe-form.ts`.\n\n\n---------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n## Serverside Example\n\nSee [./example/ssr.ts](./example/ssr.ts) for an example of rendering an HTML\nstring and then \"hydrating\" the page on the client.\n\n> [!NOTE]  \n> The server must know how to render the HTML that the components depend on.\n\n### `.TAG`\n\nEach tag name is exposed as a property `.TAG`. You can import the web\ncomponents in Node, even though Node does not have browser APIs.\n\n```ts\nimport { MyCounter, CountBtn, CopyBtn } from './index.js'\n\n// this runs in Node\n\nexport function render ():string {\n    return `<div>\n        <${MyCounter.TAG} start=\"${START}\">\n            <div data-ref=\"${MyCounter.refs.display}\"\n                role=\"status\"\n                class=\"count\"\n            >${START}</div>\n\n            <div class=\"controls\">\n                <${CountBtn.TAG}\n                    class=\"dec\"\n                    data-ref=\"${MyCounter.refs.dec}\"\n                    aria-label=\"Decrement\"\n                >\n                    <button>-</button>\n22:| `microtags/htm` | <!-- size:htm -->1.23 KB<!-- /size:htm --> |\n81:  * [`microtags/htm`](#microtagshtm)\n1336:### `microtags/htm`\n1343:import { html, raw } from 'microtags/htm'\n```ts\ntype Attrs = Record<\n    string,\n    undefined|null|string|number|boolean|(string|number)[]\n>\n\n/**\n * Transform an object into an HTML attributes string. The object should be\n * like `{ attributeName: value }`.\n *\n * @param {Attrs} attrs An object for the attributes.\n * @returns {string} A string suitable for use as HTML attributes.\n */\nfunction toAttributes (attrs:Attrs):string\n```\n\n### `microtags/htm`\n\nA tagged-template string renderer that will expand any microtags\ninstances if finds. Exports `html`, `h`, and `raw`. Works in Node and the\nbrowser -- `html` always returns a string.\n\n```ts\nimport { html, raw } from 'microtags/htm'\nimport { MyCounter } from './components.js'\n\nconst page = html`<div>\n    <${MyCounter} start=${5}>\n        <p>Extra children</p>\n    </${MyCounter}>\n    ${raw('<b>trusted markup</b>')}\n</div>`\n```\n\nWhen `html` meets a microtags element class, it splits props from\npassthrough attributes using the class's static `props` list, joins\nchildren into one string, and calls the static `render`. Plain string\ntag names emit ordinary HTML.\n\n**Escaping.** Every interpolated string is escaped (`<`, `>`, `&`, `\"`,\n`'`) before the parser sees it. Component output and `raw()` output\n57:`string | Markup`; the static `render` still returns a string.\n62:`<!--[-->`/`<!--]-->` and plain strings it returns are escaped there,\n184:holds exactly one `<!--microtags:main-->` marker; `server/scaffold.ts`\n191:`pages/`, where `pages/routes.ts` maps a route to its page (the\n233:body, state)` requires exactly one of each marker. Build the payload","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d134e0b9-0655-44e9-9843-19fd47b4c489","uuid":"d64c6583-378a-414e-9698-a611a207f22c","timestamp":"2026-10-05T00:09:18.501Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"The error stays hidden until the field is blurred once, then updates live,\nand the submit button is disabled until valid. See `example/subscribe-form.ts`.\n\n\n---------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n## Serverside Example\n\nSee [./example/ssr.ts](./example/ssr.ts) for an example of rendering an HTML\nstring and then \"hydrating\" the page on the client.\n\n> [!NOTE]  \n> The server must know how to render the HTML that the components depend on.\n\n### `.TAG`\n\nEach tag name is exposed as a property `.TAG`. You can import the web\ncomponents in Node, even though Node does not have browser APIs.\n\n```ts\nimport { MyCounter, CountBtn, CopyBtn } from './index.js'\n\n// this runs in Node\n\nexport function render ():string {\n    return `<div>\n        <${MyCounter.TAG} start=\"${START}\">\n            <div data-ref=\"${MyCounter.refs.display}\"\n                role=\"status\"\n                class=\"count\"\n            >${START}</div>\n\n            <div class=\"controls\">\n                <${CountBtn.TAG}\n                    class=\"dec\"\n                    data-ref=\"${MyCounter.refs.dec}\"\n                    aria-label=\"Decrement\"\n                >\n                    <button>-</button>\n22:| `microtags/htm` | <!-- size:htm -->1.23 KB<!-- /size:htm --> |\n81:  * [`microtags/htm`](#microtagshtm)\n1336:### `microtags/htm`\n1343:import { html, raw } from 'microtags/htm'\n```ts\ntype Attrs = Record<\n    string,\n    undefined|null|string|number|boolean|(string|number)[]\n>\n\n/**\n * Transform an object into an HTML attributes string. The object should be\n * like `{ attributeName: value }`.\n *\n * @param {Attrs} attrs An object for the attributes.\n * @returns {string} A string suitable for use as HTML attributes.\n */\nfunction toAttributes (attrs:Attrs):string\n```\n\n### `microtags/htm`\n\nA tagged-template string renderer that will expand any microtags\ninstances if finds. Exports `html`, `h`, and `raw`. Works in Node and the\nbrowser -- `html` always returns a string.\n\n```ts\nimport { html, raw } from 'microtags/htm'\nimport { MyCounter } from './components.js'\n\nconst page = html`<div>\n    <${MyCounter} start=${5}>\n        <p>Extra children</p>\n    </${MyCounter}>\n    ${raw('<b>trusted markup</b>')}\n</div>`\n```\n\nWhen `html` meets a microtags element class, it splits props from\npassthrough attributes using the class's static `props` list, joins\nchildren into one string, and calls the static `render`. Plain string\ntag names emit ordinary HTML.\n\n**Escaping.** Every interpolated string is escaped (`<`, `>`, `&`, `\"`,\n`'`) before the parser sees it. Component output and `raw()` output\n57:`string | Markup`; the static `render` still returns a string.\n62:`<!--[-->`/`<!--]-->` and plain strings it returns are escaped there,\n184:holds exactly one `<!--microtags:main-->` marker; `server/scaffold.ts`\n191:`pages/`, where `pages/routes.ts` maps a route to its page (the\n233:body, state)` requires exactly one of each marker. Build the payload","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
