{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012V9fNLKNPUCjinZA5MZsi7","type":"tool_result","content":"`'`) before the parser sees it. Component output and `raw()` output\nare trusted and never re-escaped. Static template text is trusted.\n\n**Arrays.** Array children (from `.map()`) are flattened automatically.\n\n**Void elements.** Write void tags in the self-closing form, like\n`<br />`, `<img src=\"x\" />`, and `<input value=${v} />`. The output has\nno closing tag and no trailing slash, eg `<br>`. The `htm` parser does\nnot know which tags are void, so an unclosed `<br>` is treated as an\nopen tag and swallows the content after it.\n\n**Custom elements.** A component tag always gets a closing tag in the\noutput, eg `<my-counter start=\"5\">...</my-counter>`, because HTML has no\nself-closing custom elements. In a template, close a component with\n`</${MyComponent}>` or with the `htm` shorthand `<//>`, which closes\nthe nearest open tag without repeating its name.\n\n---\n\n### `microtags/build`\n\nNode-only. Strips [`.render()`](#builderrenderfn-options) calls from\ndefine chains so the client bundle contains only hydration code.\nRequires `typescript` as a peer dependency.\n\n```ts\nimport { transform } from 'microtags/build'\n\nconst result = transform(source, {\n    keep: ['my-notice'],   // keep these tags' render in the bundle\n    cascade: true,         // dead-import removal, default false\n    filename: 'app.ts',    // shown in warnings\n})\n\nconsole.log(result.code)\nfor (const w of result.warnings) {\n    console.warn(`${w.file}:${w.line} ${w.message}`)\n}\n```\n\n**Strip rule:** a `.render(...)` call is removed when it is a link in a\n`test/index.ts` and `test/ssr.ts` import from these paths, so moves\nmust update them too.\n\n`example-hydration/index.html` is the checked-in scaffold. `<main>`\nholds exactly one `<!--microtags:main-->` marker; `server/scaffold.ts`\n`assemble` throws on zero or several markers and replaces via a\ncallback so `$&` stays literal. `server/app.ts` exports `createApp`\nwith an injectable `loadScaffold` and must stay free of Node imports.\nNothing may write to `index.html` (the old ssr-to-file scripts are\ngone). `npm run test:hydration` drives the app via `app.request()`.\nRoutes live in `server/app.ts`; each renders `Layout(state, page)` from","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d134e0b9-0655-44e9-9843-19fd47b4c489","uuid":"145339db-1109-4077-b32b-d769ea6569be","timestamp":"2026-10-05T00:09:21.965Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"`'`) before the parser sees it. Component output and `raw()` output\nare trusted and never re-escaped. Static template text is trusted.\n\n**Arrays.** Array children (from `.map()`) are flattened automatically.\n\n**Void elements.** Write void tags in the self-closing form, like\n`<br />`, `<img src=\"x\" />`, and `<input value=${v} />`. The output has\nno closing tag and no trailing slash, eg `<br>`. The `htm` parser does\nnot know which tags are void, so an unclosed `<br>` is treated as an\nopen tag and swallows the content after it.\n\n**Custom elements.** A component tag always gets a closing tag in the\noutput, eg `<my-counter start=\"5\">...</my-counter>`, because HTML has no\nself-closing custom elements. In a template, close a component with\n`</${MyComponent}>` or with the `htm` shorthand `<//>`, which closes\nthe nearest open tag without repeating its name.\n\n---\n\n### `microtags/build`\n\nNode-only. Strips [`.render()`](#builderrenderfn-options) calls from\ndefine chains so the client bundle contains only hydration code.\nRequires `typescript` as a peer dependency.\n\n```ts\nimport { transform } from 'microtags/build'\n\nconst result = transform(source, {\n    keep: ['my-notice'],   // keep these tags' render in the bundle\n    cascade: true,         // dead-import removal, default false\n    filename: 'app.ts',    // shown in warnings\n})\n\nconsole.log(result.code)\nfor (const w of result.warnings) {\n    console.warn(`${w.file}:${w.line} ${w.message}`)\n}\n```\n\n**Strip rule:** a `.render(...)` call is removed when it is a link in a\n`test/index.ts` and `test/ssr.ts` import from these paths, so moves\nmust update them too.\n\n`example-hydration/index.html` is the checked-in scaffold. `<main>`\nholds exactly one `<!--microtags:main-->` marker; `server/scaffold.ts`\n`assemble` throws on zero or several markers and replaces via a\ncallback so `$&` stays literal. `server/app.ts` exports `createApp`\nwith an injectable `loadScaffold` and must stay free of Node imports.\nNothing may write to `index.html` (the old ssr-to-file scripts are\ngone). `npm run test:hydration` drives the app via `app.request()`.\nRoutes live in `server/app.ts`; each renders `Layout(state, page)` from","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
