{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfi7rx13tCGd7m36G7KJg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JYkZTrbDTkoAc354y33xif","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/nick/code/microtags.unidirectional-hydration-13-docs-and-adr-notes; python3 - <<'EOF'\np='example-hydration/README.md'; s=open(p).read()\ndef r(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert a in s, a\n    s=s.replace(a,b)\nr(\"\"\"- `npm run test:e2e` -- Playwright tests against the production server.\n\"\"\",\"\"\"- `npm run test:e2e` -- Playwright tests against the production server.\n- `npm run toc:hydration` -- regenerate this file's table of contents.\n\"\"\")\nr(\"\"\"The routes are `/example-hydration/` (a counter with a nested badge),\n`/example-hydration/list` (badges rendered from an array), and\n`/example-hydration/notice` (a button that inserts a client-rendered\nnotice). Any other path under the prefix returns a 404 page.\"\"\",\"\"\"The routes are `/example-hydration/` (a counter with a nested badge),\n`/example-hydration/list` (a keyed list of badges with add and remove\ncontrols), and `/example-hydration/notice` (a notice shown and dismissed\nthrough state). Any other path under the prefix returns a 404 page. The\nindex route accepts a `count` query parameter when it is a finite\ninteger, for example `/example-hydration/?count=10`.\n\n## State\n\n`state.ts` runs on both sides. `State(input)` builds an `AppState`, one\nsignal per JSON value (`route`, `count`, `noticeOpen`, `labels`), and\nfills defaults for missing keys. Signals are written only through the\nstatic functions on `State`, such as `State.increase(state)`.\n`serialize(state)` returns the plain JSON form, typed as\n`Serialized<AppState>`.\n\nThe server builds state for each request, renders the page from it, and\nwrites `serialize(state)` into the document as a JSON script with the id\n`STATE_ID`. The browser reads that script, calls `State` with it, and\nmounts the same layout and page over the server-rendered DOM. From then\non a state change updates the parts of the DOM that depend on it. Routing\nstays on the server: every link is a full page load.\"\"\")\nr(\"\"\"- `index.html` -- the checked-in page scaffold, and the Vite HTML entry.\n  `<main>` holds exactly one `<!--microtags:main-->` marker, which the\n  server replaces with the route body. Nothing writes to this file.\"\"\",\"\"\"- `index.html` -- the checked-in page scaffold, and the Vite HTML entry.\n  It has two markers, each exactly once. `<div id=\"root\">` holds\n  `<!--microtags:main-->`, which the server replaces with the rendered\n  layout and page. `<!--microtags:state-->`, before the module script,\n  is replaced with the state script. Nothing writes to this file.\n- `state.ts` -- the shared app state, described [above](#state).\"\"\")\nr(\"\"\"- `index.ts` -- the client entry. It imports the components, which\n  registers them and hydrates the page, then runs a few runtime\n  assertions and prints the results on the page. The assertions check\n  that `Counter.render` and `Badge.render` are `undefined` in the\n  browser bundle and that `Notice.render` is still a function.\n- `reveal.ts` -- removes the class that hides the page until it has\n  hydrated.\"\"\",\"\"\"- `index.ts` -- the client entry. It imports the components, which\n  registers them, reads the state script, and mounts the layout into\n  `#root`. It also runs a few runtime assertions and prints the results\n  on the page: `Counter.render` is `undefined` in the browser bundle,\n  and `Notice.render` and `Badge.render` are still functions.\n- `util.ts` -- `reveal`, which removes the class that hides the page\n  until its components are defined.\"\"\")\nr(\"\"\"- `counter.ts` -- a counter with increment and decrement buttons. Its\n  `.render` returns `html`, nests a `Badge` that shows the current\n  count, and passes `children` through.\n- `badge.ts` -- the smallest possible component.\n- `notice.ts` -- keeps its render function on the client with\n  `{ client: true }`.\"\"\",\"\"\"- `counter.ts` -- a view of a `count` prop it does not own. Its buttons\n  emit `increment` and `decrement`. Its `.render` nests a `Badge`, and\n  its setup binds a derived value to that badge's `label` prop. Its\n  render is stripped.\n- `badge.ts` -- shows its `label` prop. Kept with `{ client: true }`\n  because the list page creates badges in the browser.\n- `notice.ts` -- a message whose dismiss button emits `dismiss`. Kept\n  with `{ client: true }`.\"\"\")\nr(\"\"\"The static `render` then exists in the browser, so `html` can render\nthe component on the client. `client/index.ts` does exactly this\nwhen the \"Show notice\" button is clicked:\n\n```ts\nimport { html } from 'microtags/htm'\nimport { Notice } from '../components/notice.js'\n\ntarget.innerHTML = html`<${Notice} message=${'Saved'} />`\n```\"\"\",\"\"\"The static `render` then exists in the browser, so the browser can\ncreate the component. `pages/notice.ts` shows the notice in a reactive\nregion driven by state:\n\n```ts\nhtml`${() => state.noticeOpen() ?\n    html`<${Notice} message=${'Saved'}\n        ondismiss=${() => State.dismissNotice(state)} />` :\n    null}`\n```\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncat example-hydration/pages/notice.ts | head -30"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1311,"cache_read_input_tokens":64184,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1311},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d134e0b9-0655-44e9-9843-19fd47b4c489","uuid":"7ae4aa3f-98cc-41a7-9ed4-50f328dbe046","timestamp":"2026-10-05T00:10:02.623Z","request_id":"req_011Cfi7rwBBAtwxTrKMXJWp8","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01J