{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfi7xs2pWhVUjM9R517LR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] The glossary defines markup, mount, reactive region, and adopt, and the four revised entries match the shipped behaviour\n[x] The example README names every hydration npm script and every directory that exists, and its table of contents is regenerated\n[x] AGENTS.md no longer describes `html` as returning a plain string, `server/routes.ts`, or a single scaffold marker\n[x] ADR-005 and ADR-006 each carry the note described above and are not marked superseded\n[x] No doc states that a host's attribute reflects the current value of a signal-bound prop\n[x] `npm run lint` passes with `example-hydration/build/` deleted\n\nThe docs now match what shipped. `npm run lint` passes with `example-hydration/build/` deleted, and the full `npm test` run passed 286 of 286. There are two commits: `e08f8cd` (lint fix) and `057e6bf` (docs).\n\n1. **Glossary (`CONTEXT.md`):** added **Markup**, **Reactive region**, **Mount** and **Adopt**. Revised **Templater**, **Trusted string**, **Hydration** and **Prop**. The **Prop** entry now says that once a signal is assigned to a prop, the host's attribute no longer reflects its value. **Template** still means only the native `<template>` element. I also changed **Render function** to say it returns a string or markup.\n2. **Example README:** added a State section and an entry for `state.ts`. It now describes the scaffold's two markers and the `#root` wrapper, and lists `toc:hydration`. I corrected the stale entries: the client file is `util.ts`, not `reveal.ts`, and the counter, badge, notice, routes and runtime-assertion descriptions now match the code. The kept-render example was replaced with the region pattern from `pages/notice.ts`. The table of contents is regenerated.\n3. **`AGENTS.md`:** the scaffold paragraph now covers both markers and the \"exactly once\" rule. A new paragraph says Badge and Notice keep their render and Counter is stripped, gives Counter's `count` prop and its events, and repeats the attribute caveat. The browser templater's size-limit entry was already documented, so I left it alone.\n4. **ADR-005 and ADR-006:** each has a dated note (the markup return type and kept components; the state marker and root wrapper). Neither is marked superseded.\n5. **Top-level `README.md`:** only the `microtags/htm` sentence that said `html` \"always returns a string\" changed.\n\nI made one change outside the ticket's file list. Lint was already failing on `HEAD` with two unused-variable errors in `test/plugins.ts`. Since the ticket requires lint to pass, I prefixed those two names with `_`. That doesn't change how the tests behave, and it's in its own commit if you'd rather handle it differently.\n\nThe worktree had no `node_modules`, so I ran `npm install` before linting. Lint failed to load until I did. No dependency files changed in the commits. I didn't add anything else to `AGENTS.md` beyond the ticket's content."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":330,"cache_read_input_tokens":72100,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":330},"output_tokens":719,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d134e0b9-0655-44e9-9843-19fd47b4c489","uuid":"3fc2e69e-7940-4cea-a0b2-089aab184167","timestamp":"2026-10-05T00:11:14.877Z","request_id":"req_011Cfi7xqw5ubRN2XjCbsc1t"}
